        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.33,
            0.37,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What does this show?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.354,
            0.846,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A path on the surface of the cuboid can be transformed to a path of the same length on the net. Conversely, every path on the net transforms to a path of the same length on the cuboid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.41,
            0.845,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the first case, the path marked on the cuboid is the shortest since it transforms to a straight line between the ant and laddu on the net, which is the shortest path between them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.464,
            0.846,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the second case, the path marked on the cuboid does not transform to a straight line path on the net, and hence is not the shortest path for the ant to take."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.538,
            0.84,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.159,
                0.538,
                0.84,
                0.758
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.598,
            0.577,
            0.842,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Laddu",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (at the centre of the edge)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.758,
            0.599,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The red path is the shortest"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.787,
            0.845,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, by using a net, we convert the problem of finding the shortest path on a cuboid to the problem of finding the shortest path on the net."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.824,
            0.846,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Have we now completely analysed the problem of finding the shortest path between two points on a cuboid?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
